AB  - The primary objective of the study is to study the change in SpA disease activity, according to ASAS20 definition (Anderson et al., 2001), after 8 weeks of VNS treatment versus placebo non-specific stimulation (control group).
AB  - The secondary objectives of the Clinical Investigation are to show differences in disease evolution between the active and placebo periods of 8 weeks treatment with active VNS versus placebo VNS of the following items:
AB  - 1. Change in disease activity according to "ASAS40" criteria
AB  - 2. Obtaining a partial remission according to the ASAS definition
AB  - 3. Change in BASFI
AB  - 4. Change in C-reactive protein (CRP)serum level and erythrocytes sedimentation rate (ESR),
AB  - 5. Change in ASDAS_CRP and ASDAS_ESR
AB  - 6. Difference in levels of circulating cytokines, IL-6, IL-23, IL-17, IL-33 and of matrix metallopeptidases (MMP3-8-9).
AB  - 7. Change in quality of life : assessment according to the following indexes: SF-36, AS Quality of Life (ASQOL)
AB  - 8. Change in Health Index of patient with SpA (ASAS HI) and of the Productivity at Work Index (WPI)
AB  - 9. Change in fatigue (BASDAI 1st question) and global pain
AB  - 10. Change in Anxiety and Depression Assessment (HAD)
AB  - 11. Change in BASMI
AB  - 12. Change in non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAID) intake score.
