AB  - Multimodal analgesia (MMA) has been endorsed to improve postoperative analgesia and functional activity after surgery, and integrating regional analgesia to reduce the consumption of opioid has also been used in postoperative pain management. The investigator try to find a better combination of MMA for postoperative analgesia and functional recovery for patients receiving TKA in Taiwan, therefore the effect of single-injection and continuous infusion of peripheral nerve block is compared in patient undergoing unilateral TKA. The investigators hypothesize that continuous adductor canal infusion is as effective as single-injection adductor canal block for postoperative pain relief under intravenous PCA after TKA surgery. Based on that, the investigators conduct this prospective, randomized controlled trial to examine our hypothesis.
