AB  - The purpose of the proposed study is to determine if pairing reactivation of a traumatic memory with a single administration of Rapamycin (e.g., Sirolimus) in men with combat-related Posttraumatic Stress Disorder leads to a reduction of the emotional strength of that particular traumatic memory.
AB  - The following hypotheses will be tested:
AB  - 1. Traumatic memory reactivation paired with a single dose of Rapamycin will decrease objective measures of stress and self-report of stress during replay of the traumatic memory, relative to, subjects receiving placebo.
AB  - 2. Pairing administration of Rapamycin with traumatic memory reactivation will decrease symptoms of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder one month and three months later, relative to patients receiving placebo.
