AB  - The goal of this clinical trial is to investigate the biological pathways underlying the beneficial effect of omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids (n-3 PUFA) on mental health in patients with alcohol use disorder. The main questions this study aims to answer are:
AB  - - Can n-3 PUFA improve mood disorders (depression, anxiety), craving for alcohol, cognitive impairments and sociability disorders ?
AB  - - Are the beneficial effects of n-3 PUFAs due to a modification of the gut microbiota and/or the inflammatory status?
AB  - Participants will :
AB  - - take a supplementation of omega-3 or placebo during 3 months
AB  - - do a brain MRI
AB  - - be interviewed for a dietary anamnesis
AB  - - provide blood, stool and saliva samples
AB  - - perform psychological tests and neuropsychological tasks
AB  - Researchers will compare active comparator (omega-3) with placebo comparator (olive oil) to see if omega-3 can have a beneficial effect on AUD patients.
AN  - NCT05899660
SF  - ClinicalTrials.gov
ST  - Impact of Omega 3 in Alcohol Use Disorder (W3-AUD)
TI  - Impact of Omega-3 Polyunsaturated Fatty Acids on Emotional, Cognitive and Biological Alterations in Alcohol Use Disorder
