AB  - Primary Objective:
AB  - To demonstrate the benefit of isatuximab in combination with pomalidomide and low-dose dexamethasone in the prolongation of Progression Free Survival (PFS) as compared to pomalidomide and low-dose dexamethasone in participants with refractory or relapsed and refractory multiple myeloma (MM).
AB  - Secondary Objectives:
AB  - - To evaluate the Overall Response Rate (ORR) as per International Myeloma Working Group (IMWG) criteria in each arm.
AB  - - To compare the Overall Survival (OS) between the two arms.
AB  - - To evaluate the Time To Progression (TTP) in each arm.
AB  - - To evaluate the PFS in high risk cytogenetic population in each arm.
AB  - - To evaluate the Duration of Response (DOR) in each arm.
AB  - - To evaluate the safety in both treatment arms.
AB  - - To determine the Pharmacokinetic profile of isatuximab in combination with pomalidomide.
AB  - - To evaluate the immunogenicity of isatuximab.
AB  - - To assess disease-specific and generic health-related quality of life (HRQL), disease and treatment-related symptoms, health state utility, and health status.
AN  - NCT02990338
