ID  - 5286918
AB  - Objectives:
AB  - To determine whether CRP-guided antibiotic treatment for managing AECOPD in adult patients attending Emergency Departments leads to reduced antibiotic duration, without non-inferior COPD health status with usual care.
AB  - Hypothesis to be tested:
AB  - (i) The antibiotic duration in AECOPD patients will be significantly lower for CRP-guided antibiotic discontinuation than usual care; and (ii) COPD health status as measured by the Clinical COPD Questionnaire has no statistically significant difference between two groups.
AB  - Design and subjects:
AB  - Multi-center, single-blind, open-label, randomized, combined superiority (antibiotic duration) and non-inferiority (COPD health status) trial in 1,184 adult AECOPD patients presented to A&E.
AB  - Instruments:
AB  - Clinical COPD Questionnaire and EuroQol-5D
AB  - Interventions:
AB  - Both intervention and control groups follow usual care with GOLD strategy. The intervention group will be recommended to test for serum CRP daily. Antibiotic prescription is considered when CRP >5mg/dL. Once CRP has declined to <5mg/dL and the patient was afebrile for past 48 hours, antibiotic discontinuation will be considered.
AB  - Communication with Receiving Ward Staffs:
AB  - Participants in the study may transfer to another departments after treatment/ care in A&E. The following communication would be conducted:
AB  - - A handover note that informs the receiving ward staffs about patients' enrolment to the trial, group assignment, and previous treatments given in A&E. The note would also suggest the investigations for the receiving ward staffs.
AB  - - Telephone handover about intervention group and investigations of the study, and treatments given in A&E to ward.
AB  - Main outcome measures:
AB  - The antibiotic duration (total number of antibiotic days) within 28 days and recovery in terms of COPD health status (Clinical COPD Questionnaire total scores) within 14 days from randomisation.
AB  - Data analysis:
AB  - Intention-to-treat and cost-effectiveness analyses will be performed. The outcome assessors and data analysts will be blinded to group allocation.
AB  - Expected results:
AB  - The intervention group will exhibit reduction in antibiotic duration at 4-weeks, without negatively impacting on COPD health status, compared with the control group.
AN  - NCT05286918
SF  - ClinicalTrials.gov
ST  - Antibiotic Stewardship in AECOPD Through CRP-Guided Management
TI  - Antibiotic Stewardship Through CRP-guided Antibiotic Treatment for Patients With Acute Exacerbation of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (AECOPD)
