AB  - Primary Objective:
AB  - To demonstrate whether an early fixed Somatostatin treatment improves the complete recovery rate of early postoperative simple small bowel obstruction (EPSSBO) compared with the common daily practice
AB  - Notes:
AB  - 1. complete recovery= toleration of solid food+ flatus+ passage+ recovery of bowel movement.
AB  - 2. common daily practice includes:
AB  - 2.- NPO (Nil per mouth), re-dehydration, TPN (Total Parenteral Nutrition) if needed. Check & make sure stability of electrolytes daily.
AB  - 2.- GI (Gastro-Intestinal) depression via NGT (Naso-Gastric Tube)
AB  - 2.- Discontinue opiates, instead of NSAIDs. (Non-Steroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drugs)
AB  - 2.- Pro-dynamic drugs or other drugs which may interfere with GI (Gastro-Intestinal) movement eg. anti-histamines, anti-cholinergic, opiates, anti-depressives are not indicated.
AB  - Secondary Objectives:
AB  - To investigate whether an early fixed Somatostatin treatment will bring much benefit to EPSSBO pts compared with the common daily practice,for this purpose,the study will investigate the endpoints below.
