AB  - The goal of this clinical trial is to assess the effectiveness of a cerclage in women with a twin pregnancy with a midpregnancy short cervix or cervical dilatation compared to standard treatment (no cerclage) in the prevention of extreme preterm birth < 28 weeks of gestational age.
AB  - The main question it aims to answer is: What is the effectiveness of a cerclage in women with a twin pregnancy with a midpregnancy short cervix or cervical dilatation compared to standard treatment (no cerclage) in the prevention of extreme preterm birth < 28 weeks of gestational age?
AB  - Participants will be randomly assigned to the intervention (cerclage) or comparison (no cerclage) group.
