AB  - The purpose of this project is to conduct a pilot study evaluating the feasibility and potential benefits of a phone assessment/reporting system (tele-system) in addition to a written action plan and nurse case manager support to improve patients' adherence to COPD treatment in those at risk for exacerbations.
AB  - Primary objective: explore the potential benefits with respect to patient's adherence, i.e., prompt use of the antibiotic and/or prednisone in the event of an exacerbation, increased adherence to maintenance medication; to increase patient's self-efficacy" in self-managing their disease; and to use more efficiently program resources, i.e., the case-manager.
AB  - Secondary objectives:
AB  - To assess the proportion of patients who effectively self manage exacerbations by using their COPD Action Plan
AB  - To assess self management of COPD patients with respect to the increased adherence to regular respiratory medication, (SmartInhaler electronic monitoring);
AB  - To assess increased self-efficacy in COPD patients identifying and managing exacerbations (baseline vs after 12 months);
AB  - To assess symptoms recovery, health status improvement, and prevention of ER visits and hospital admissions for COPD exacerbations.
AB  - To assess the efficiency in using program resources,
AB  - To evaluate the feasibility of this treatment approach and to provide pilot data (needed for a larger multi-centre clinical trial;
AB  - To evaluate the feasibility and need of assessment during and after exacerbation onset, health-related quality of life and physical activity;
AB  - To evaluate the safety of this approach; this is in terms of the delay in starting prednisone and an unfavourable outcome (ER visits and/or hospitalization).
AN  - NCT02275078
SF  - ClinicalTrials.gov
ST  - Innovations in Treating COPD Exacerbations: Pilot Project on Action Plans Using New Technology.
TI  - Pilot Study Evaluating the Feasibility and Potential Benefits of a Novel Approach of COPD Self-management That Includes a Phone Assessment/Reporting System (Tele-system)
