AB  - The goal of this clinical trial is to test the ability to restore gut microbiota to healthier levels in patients with blood cancers scheduled to have stem cell transplant.
AB  - The main questions it aims to answer are:
AB  - - Tolerability and acceptability of intestinal microbiota transplantation (IMT) versus placebo (as assessed via patient perspective questionnaires
AB  - - Changes in gut microbiome diversity across all timepoints
AB  - - Markers of general health, infective/microbiological and haematological outcomes including, days of fever, admission to intensive care unit, survival, non-relapsed mortality, and incidence of graft-versus-host disease across all time points measured.
AB  - Participants will be asked at their routine follow up visits to,
AB  - - Provide stool, urine and blood samples at the scheduled study visits
AB  - - Complete questionnaires at selected visits
AB  - - Swallow either Placebo or IMT capsules once at the second study visit which will occur 2 weeks prior to the stem cell transplant (+/-3 days)
AB  - Researchers will compare IMT capsules and Placebo to investigate the change in gut microbiota diversity.
AN  - NCT06355583
